1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:03,628
♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor… ♪

2
00:00:06,005 --> 00:00:08,508
["Mamang Sastre" playing]

3
00:00:08,591 --> 00:00:10,802
(Fix this) ♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor ♪

4
00:00:10,885 --> 00:00:12,929
♪ Holding the scissors ♪

5
00:00:13,012 --> 00:00:16,641
♪ One cut, and it's over ♪

6
00:00:17,350 --> 00:00:18,309
You're really lucky, buddy.

7
00:00:18,393 --> 00:00:21,354
You have a family; you have a business.

8
00:00:21,438 --> 00:00:24,315
Someday you'll find everything you're
looking for too.

9
00:00:24,399 --> 00:00:25,734
Thank you, buddy.

10
00:00:26,317 --> 00:00:27,569
What's this we're hearing,

11
00:00:27,652 --> 00:00:31,614
that your Brother Atoy and
Audrey are fighting?

12
00:00:31,698 --> 00:00:34,284
Audrey mistook Oscar for a bad person.

13
00:00:34,367 --> 00:00:36,202
Mistaken identity?

14
00:00:36,286 --> 00:00:39,497
EMERSON: I get a different vibe
from him that's… not good.

15
00:00:39,581 --> 00:00:41,166
No, because it's like
you look like someone.

16
00:00:41,249 --> 00:00:42,542
Hmm? Who?

17
00:00:42,625 --> 00:00:45,378
Our future firstborn. [giggles]

18
00:00:45,462 --> 00:00:47,672
Audrey: I already warned him about Oscar.

19
00:00:47,756 --> 00:00:48,798
But he really won't listen.

20
00:00:48,882 --> 00:00:51,843
He wouldn't be Atoy's friend
if he were bad.

21
00:00:51,926 --> 00:00:53,720
Do you know anything about Belladonna?

22
00:00:53,803 --> 00:00:55,305
Even though I was imprisoned there,

23
00:00:55,388 --> 00:00:56,806
they wouldn't have let me hear
things like that.

24
00:00:56,890 --> 00:01:01,895
Samir: I think it is time to go
visit our prisoners.

25
00:01:01,978 --> 00:01:03,897
We will make them tell us

26
00:01:03,980 --> 00:01:05,565
who Belladonna is.

27
00:01:05,648 --> 00:01:07,442
Of all the missions

28
00:01:07,525 --> 00:01:08,818
you and Atoy went on,

29
00:01:08,902 --> 00:01:10,904
which one will you never forget?

30
00:01:10,987 --> 00:01:11,863
A rescue mission,

31
00:01:11,946 --> 00:01:13,448
he abandoned me.

32
00:01:13,531 --> 00:01:16,034
He left me there to die.

33
00:01:16,117 --> 00:01:17,577
I didn't leave you.

34
00:01:17,660 --> 00:01:19,120
- Come on, I'll take you
- Both: Oh!

35
00:01:19,204 --> 00:01:20,830
[thumps & squeals]

36
00:01:20,914 --> 00:01:22,040
OTHERS: Hey!

37
00:01:22,123 --> 00:01:23,166
- [growls]
- [gasps]

38
00:01:23,249 --> 00:01:24,083
[growling & grunting]

39
00:01:24,167 --> 00:01:25,418
[thumping]

40
00:01:26,211 --> 00:01:27,754
ATOY: He's still upset with me,

41
00:01:27,837 --> 00:01:29,088
because of what I did,

42
00:01:29,172 --> 00:01:30,340
leaving him behind.

43
00:01:30,423 --> 00:01:32,801
[music swells]

44
00:01:36,513 --> 00:01:37,472
[music fades]

45
00:01:38,389 --> 00:01:40,266
[birds & crickets chirping
in the distance]

46
00:01:40,350 --> 00:01:41,184
[car door closes]

47
00:01:44,646 --> 00:01:45,814
Oh?

48
00:01:45,897 --> 00:01:47,273
Why is Janine running like that?

49
00:01:48,316 --> 00:01:49,943
- Psst.
- Ibyang: Ah.

50
00:01:50,026 --> 00:01:53,363
Hmm, Janine is in a hurry to go inside.

51
00:01:53,988 --> 00:01:55,281
She went to the CR.

52
00:01:55,365 --> 00:01:56,991
[chuckles] Went to the CR?

53
00:01:57,075 --> 00:01:59,077
Eh, why doesn't she go to the CR at home?

54
00:01:59,911 --> 00:02:02,247
Just give her this lunch box, okay.

55
00:02:02,330 --> 00:02:03,456
Yes.

56
00:02:04,999 --> 00:02:06,960
Ah, Tatoy.

57
00:02:07,043 --> 00:02:09,629
Miss Cita said that…

58
00:02:10,380 --> 00:02:11,798
Uncle Oscar will be staying

59
00:02:11,881 --> 00:02:13,424
at the tailoring shop?

60
00:02:15,135 --> 00:02:15,969
Not anymore.

61
00:02:16,553 --> 00:02:17,679
He left last night,

62
00:02:17,762 --> 00:02:19,472
and it seems he won't be coming back.

63
00:02:19,556 --> 00:02:21,558
What will happen now?

64
00:02:22,642 --> 00:02:23,476
Hmm.

65
00:02:23,560 --> 00:02:26,020
Tatoy has no friend anymore.

66
00:02:26,980 --> 00:02:28,148
That’s sad.

67
00:02:28,231 --> 00:02:30,984
Child, that really happens in friendships.

68
00:02:32,235 --> 00:02:33,862
Because your Uncle Oscar and I

69
00:02:34,654 --> 00:02:36,322
haven't been together for a long time.

70
00:02:36,406 --> 00:02:38,491
We hadn't seen each other in
a long time, so it's like--

71
00:02:38,575 --> 00:02:40,243
You know? We drifted apart.

72
00:02:40,952 --> 00:02:41,953
So, you…

73
00:02:42,537 --> 00:02:45,081
I want you to value your friends.

74
00:02:45,165 --> 00:02:47,959
But before that, value your sister,
Janine, first.

75
00:02:48,042 --> 00:02:50,461
Then value those who are kind to you here,

76
00:02:50,545 --> 00:02:51,629
especially the true friends.

77
00:02:51,713 --> 00:02:52,672
Okay?

78
00:02:53,298 --> 00:02:54,340
Yes.

79
00:02:54,424 --> 00:02:57,802
And we won't drift apart, Janine and I,

80
00:02:57,886 --> 00:03:00,430
because she is the needle to my thread.

81
00:03:00,513 --> 00:03:01,681
Nice. I like that.

82
00:03:01,764 --> 00:03:02,974
Needle to thread. Hmm?

83
00:03:03,057 --> 00:03:04,559
- HAILEY: Ibyang!
- Huh?

84
00:03:05,101 --> 00:03:06,603
- Hello!
- Hi!

85
00:03:07,645 --> 00:03:08,605
Hailey: Is he your father?

86
00:03:08,688 --> 00:03:09,856
Oh, yes.

87
00:03:09,939 --> 00:03:12,191
Oh, yes. I'm her father.

88
00:03:12,275 --> 00:03:14,152
Hello, sir! I'm Hailey!

89
00:03:14,235 --> 00:03:16,112
Ibyang and Janine helped me find my cat,

90
00:03:16,195 --> 00:03:17,488
and Mr. Emerson too!

91
00:03:18,156 --> 00:03:19,991
Oh, Frankie?

92
00:03:20,074 --> 00:03:21,451
He was yours!

93
00:03:21,534 --> 00:03:22,785
Both: Tamago!

94
00:03:22,869 --> 00:03:24,287
Oh, sorry. Sorry for that.

95
00:03:24,370 --> 00:03:26,205
Tamago, it's Tamago.

96
00:03:27,123 --> 00:03:29,542
Okay, go on. Go inside. Oh, behave, okay.

97
00:03:29,626 --> 00:03:31,753
Yes. Bye-bye!

98
00:03:32,253 --> 00:03:33,630
- Hmm.
- [smooches]

99
00:03:34,255 --> 00:03:35,340
- Bye, sir!
- Bye-bye.

100
00:03:35,423 --> 00:03:36,466
Can we be friends now?

101
00:03:36,549 --> 00:03:38,843
You, me and Janine?

102
00:03:39,385 --> 00:03:41,930
Okay! Suman! Mmm-mmm.

103
00:03:42,013 --> 00:03:42,972
What's suman?

104
00:03:43,765 --> 00:03:46,976
Suman is, ah…

105
00:03:47,060 --> 00:03:50,188
white circle, round, cold…

106
00:03:51,439 --> 00:03:53,107
Ah, with-- with carrot nose.

107
00:03:53,191 --> 00:03:54,734
Snow-- snowman, that’s “snowman.”

108
00:03:54,817 --> 00:03:56,861
The round one, with-- snowman.

109
00:03:56,945 --> 00:03:57,904
- Oh.
- [chuckles]

110
00:03:57,987 --> 00:03:59,989
Oh you, snowman.

111
00:04:00,073 --> 00:04:01,324
Okay, then. Bye-bye.

112
00:04:01,407 --> 00:04:02,659
Bye-bye.

113
00:04:02,742 --> 00:04:04,160
- Hug.
- [playful music playing]

114
00:04:04,244 --> 00:04:05,078
Mmm.

115
00:04:05,828 --> 00:04:06,663
Ah.

116
00:04:06,746 --> 00:04:07,830
- Take care.
- Bye, sir!

117
00:04:07,914 --> 00:04:09,958
- Bye-bye, bye-bye!
- Bye, Tatoy!

118
00:04:10,541 --> 00:04:11,459
Take care.

119
00:04:11,542 --> 00:04:14,337
♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor… ♪

120
00:04:14,420 --> 00:04:17,548
["Mamang Sastre" playing]

121
00:04:19,968 --> 00:04:22,095
♪ Wait a moment, Mr. Tailor ♪

122
00:04:22,178 --> 00:04:23,429
♪ Can you be the one to stitch up ♪

123
00:04:23,513 --> 00:04:24,806
♪ The hole in my polo

124
00:04:24,889 --> 00:04:27,642
that's right under the armpit ♪

125
00:04:27,725 --> 00:04:29,060
♪ In every cut of cloth ♪

126
00:04:29,143 --> 00:04:31,396
♪ There’s a secret behind it ♪

127
00:04:31,479 --> 00:04:33,314
♪ If your measurements are wrong,

128
00:04:33,398 --> 00:04:36,985
the whole fit turns crooked… ♪

129
00:04:37,068 --> 00:04:38,569
[gunshots]

130
00:04:38,653 --> 00:04:40,321
♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor ♪

131
00:04:40,405 --> 00:04:42,323
♪ Holding the scissors ♪

132
00:04:42,407 --> 00:04:44,284
[music swells]

133
00:04:44,367 --> 00:04:45,743
(Fix this)

134
00:04:45,827 --> 00:04:47,745
[music fades]

135
00:04:49,372 --> 00:04:50,790
Oh, just take what you want.

136
00:04:50,873 --> 00:04:52,125
It's my treat!

137
00:04:52,208 --> 00:04:55,044
Sky is the limit!
But just one stick each, okay.

138
00:04:55,128 --> 00:04:56,421
Congrats, Sir!

139
00:04:56,504 --> 00:04:58,089
Danny Guo has escaped o many times.

140
00:04:58,172 --> 00:04:59,590
- You're the only ones who caught him.
- [smirks]

141
00:04:59,674 --> 00:05:01,175
No biggie.

142
00:05:01,259 --> 00:05:03,136
Imagine, that wasn't even assigned to me.

143
00:05:03,219 --> 00:05:04,095
If it had been assigned to me,

144
00:05:04,178 --> 00:05:06,014
I would have caught him sooner.

145
00:05:07,015 --> 00:05:08,933
- You're an idol, Sir!
- [scoffs]

146
00:05:09,767 --> 00:05:10,643
That's right, Sir.

147
00:05:10,727 --> 00:05:14,480
Of course, because the eel has no
escape from Matangbaka. [scoffs]

148
00:05:16,733 --> 00:05:20,445
Sir, Uno Alcaraz has been moved
to a regular room.

149
00:05:20,528 --> 00:05:22,238
Let's go, because there are people

150
00:05:22,322 --> 00:05:23,406
who want to talk to him.

151
00:05:24,282 --> 00:05:25,742
Who? Atoy?

152
00:05:26,284 --> 00:05:27,618
They didn't say.

153
00:05:27,702 --> 00:05:29,579
[suspicious music playing]

154
00:05:34,042 --> 00:05:35,418
[laptop blipping]

155
00:05:37,545 --> 00:05:39,464
Samir: What is the news?

156
00:05:39,547 --> 00:05:41,799
Sir, still no confession for this batch.

157
00:05:43,176 --> 00:05:44,927
It has been days!

158
00:05:45,011 --> 00:05:46,888
I am growing impatient.

159
00:05:46,971 --> 00:05:48,848
[suspicious music playing]

160
00:05:54,979 --> 00:05:55,897
You.

161
00:05:56,564 --> 00:05:59,984
Tell me who was hired to rescue
the Belladonna.

162
00:06:00,068 --> 00:06:02,320
[music continues]

163
00:06:02,403 --> 00:06:03,613
Speak!

164
00:06:04,489 --> 00:06:05,323
I don't know.

165
00:06:06,532 --> 00:06:08,743
Even if I did, I would never tell you.

166
00:06:09,368 --> 00:06:11,079
We protect our clients.

167
00:06:12,371 --> 00:06:13,623
Such a shame.

168
00:06:14,165 --> 00:06:16,000
You are beautiful.

169
00:06:16,709 --> 00:06:20,171
Shock her till her eyes bleed.

170
00:06:20,254 --> 00:06:21,672
She will die.

171
00:06:22,757 --> 00:06:23,800
[music swells]

172
00:06:23,883 --> 00:06:25,301
That is the point.

173
00:06:25,384 --> 00:06:27,428
[music fades] [clicking]

174
00:06:27,512 --> 00:06:28,888
[electric buzzing]

175
00:06:28,971 --> 00:06:31,265
[tense music playing]

176
00:06:33,059 --> 00:06:34,185
[music fades]

177
00:06:34,727 --> 00:06:38,272
[ominous music playing]

178
00:06:43,277 --> 00:06:44,529
Samir: You.

179
00:06:45,113 --> 00:06:46,823
It is your turn.

180
00:06:46,906 --> 00:06:50,368
Talk now or be like your friend.

181
00:06:50,952 --> 00:06:54,205
- [spits]
- [music swells]

182
00:06:57,041 --> 00:06:58,000
[gunshot]

183
00:06:58,084 --> 00:06:58,918
[wails]

184
00:07:01,963 --> 00:07:03,631
[grunts]

185
00:07:04,257 --> 00:07:05,174
Please.

186
00:07:05,758 --> 00:07:06,926
Please, I don't know

187
00:07:07,009 --> 00:07:08,761
where the Belladonna is!

188
00:07:08,845 --> 00:07:11,180
Then you will die.

189
00:07:11,264 --> 00:07:12,515
No, please.

190
00:07:12,598 --> 00:07:14,934
Wait, wait. I'll talk.

191
00:07:15,017 --> 00:07:16,686
[sobs]

192
00:07:16,769 --> 00:07:18,688
I was initially assigned

193
00:07:18,771 --> 00:07:20,523
to rescue the Belladonna but…

194
00:07:20,606 --> 00:07:21,732
But what?!

195
00:07:22,358 --> 00:07:24,569
It was given to someone else!

196
00:07:24,652 --> 00:07:26,112
[tense music playing]

197
00:07:28,489 --> 00:07:29,323
Who?

198
00:07:31,993 --> 00:07:33,578
[music swells]

199
00:07:33,661 --> 00:07:34,996
The Firefighter.

200
00:07:35,079 --> 00:07:36,581
[music intensifies]

201
00:07:36,664 --> 00:07:38,791
Who is this Firefighter?

202
00:07:38,875 --> 00:07:40,585
That's Uno Alcaraz.

203
00:07:41,377 --> 00:07:42,879
The one at the hospital.

204
00:07:43,629 --> 00:07:45,965
Then we must go right now and get him.

205
00:07:46,048 --> 00:07:48,134
[music continues]

206
00:07:48,217 --> 00:07:49,260
Please, please--

207
00:07:49,802 --> 00:07:52,472
[music swells]

208
00:07:53,264 --> 00:07:56,100
[phone ringing]

209
00:07:56,184 --> 00:07:58,519
- [phone blips]
- Oh, Karla?

210
00:07:58,603 --> 00:08:01,606
Denden and I were supposed to visit Uno,

211
00:08:01,689 --> 00:08:03,900
but they say he's no longer in the ICU?

212
00:08:03,983 --> 00:08:05,568
They say he's been moved
to a regular room.

213
00:08:05,651 --> 00:08:07,528
Oh, Uno is out of the ICU?

214
00:08:08,154 --> 00:08:08,988
They say he's stable,

215
00:08:09,071 --> 00:08:11,157
but his wounds haven't fully healed yet.

216
00:08:11,240 --> 00:08:12,992
Karla on the phone: Maybe he
can talk already.

217
00:08:14,452 --> 00:08:15,953
Find out the room number.

218
00:08:16,037 --> 00:08:17,705
I'm going over there now,
don't leave, okay.

219
00:08:17,788 --> 00:08:19,665
I need to talk to Uno. Okay?

220
00:08:19,749 --> 00:08:21,042
Okay, Big Brother. Perfect timing,

221
00:08:21,125 --> 00:08:22,502
I'm at the information desk too.

222
00:08:23,085 --> 00:08:23,961
Bye, Big Brother.

223
00:08:24,629 --> 00:08:27,757
[suspicious music playing]

224
00:08:27,840 --> 00:08:30,927
Nurse, where was Uno Alcaraz transferred?

225
00:08:31,010 --> 00:08:31,928
We're his visitors.

226
00:08:32,011 --> 00:08:33,638
He's in Room 415 now.

227
00:08:33,721 --> 00:08:35,848
But you can't just visit on a whim.

228
00:08:35,932 --> 00:08:38,059
You need clearance from the
lead investigator.

229
00:08:38,726 --> 00:08:40,019
Who is that?

230
00:08:40,102 --> 00:08:42,355
Police Captain Elias Matangbaka.

231
00:08:43,272 --> 00:08:44,857
[music swells]

232
00:09:20,101 --> 00:09:22,728
[birds chirping in distance]

233
00:09:23,396 --> 00:09:24,355
There!

234
00:09:25,022 --> 00:09:28,693
Because we are now official BFFs.

235
00:09:28,776 --> 00:09:32,029
This is our combined name now.

236
00:09:32,113 --> 00:09:33,364
Ja-Ha-Byang!

237
00:09:34,407 --> 00:09:35,283
HAILEY: What?

238
00:09:35,908 --> 00:09:36,867
Ja-Ha-Byang.

239
00:09:37,868 --> 00:09:39,036
Uhm…

240
00:09:39,120 --> 00:09:40,121
Here, look.

241
00:09:41,706 --> 00:09:43,916
Ja, Janine, for Ja.

242
00:09:44,500 --> 00:09:48,671
Ha, Hai, Hailey. Ja-Ha.

243
00:09:49,589 --> 00:09:51,924
And Byang, for Ibyang.

244
00:09:52,008 --> 00:09:53,759
- I like that.
- Ja-Ha-Byang!

245
00:09:53,843 --> 00:09:55,303
- Is that okay?
- Yeah.

246
00:09:55,386 --> 00:09:56,387
I like that.

247
00:09:56,470 --> 00:09:58,097
You're really smart, and so talented too!

248
00:09:58,180 --> 00:10:01,183
Ah, sure!

249
00:10:01,267 --> 00:10:04,270
- Uhm, can I ask you something?
- Mmm-hmm.

250
00:10:04,353 --> 00:10:06,397
You're sisters and you're the same age.

251
00:10:06,939 --> 00:10:09,275
Are you fraternal twins?

252
00:10:09,358 --> 00:10:10,526
[mellow music playing]

253
00:10:10,610 --> 00:10:12,111
Ah, because…

254
00:10:12,194 --> 00:10:13,070
Ah, yes!

255
00:10:13,154 --> 00:10:14,947
Yes, we're fraternal twins.

256
00:10:15,489 --> 00:10:17,908
Ibyang was born first, 10 seconds ahead,

257
00:10:17,992 --> 00:10:19,118
so she's the eldest.

258
00:10:19,201 --> 00:10:22,163
- HAILEY: Ohh!
- Okay.

259
00:10:22,997 --> 00:10:24,540
What about your daddy?

260
00:10:24,624 --> 00:10:25,458
Is he going to an office

261
00:10:25,541 --> 00:10:26,876
after dropping you off?

262
00:10:27,585 --> 00:10:28,878
What's his work?

263
00:10:28,961 --> 00:10:30,671
Ah, Tatoy,

264
00:10:31,172 --> 00:10:33,549
uhm, he doesn't work in an office.

265
00:10:34,383 --> 00:10:35,509
He's a sastre.

266
00:10:36,344 --> 00:10:37,762
What's sastre? What?

267
00:10:37,845 --> 00:10:40,931
Sastre is tailor in English.

268
00:10:41,557 --> 00:10:43,934
Many tailors are working for him.

269
00:10:44,810 --> 00:10:46,979
Oh! He is a businessman!

270
00:10:47,605 --> 00:10:49,065
My dad is the same!

271
00:10:49,148 --> 00:10:50,941
He has a construction company,

272
00:10:51,025 --> 00:10:52,860
and he has so many workers!

273
00:10:54,070 --> 00:10:55,196
What about your mommy?

274
00:10:55,279 --> 00:10:56,364
What does she do?

275
00:10:58,324 --> 00:11:01,327
Janine, I'll be the one to answer, okay.

276
00:11:02,244 --> 00:11:03,913
Yeah, fine. Yes.

277
00:11:04,664 --> 00:11:06,916
[music continues]

278
00:11:06,999 --> 00:11:09,543
Mommy's job, ah,

279
00:11:09,627 --> 00:11:11,879
she's an international NGO worker.

280
00:11:12,463 --> 00:11:15,466
She helps farmers

281
00:11:16,801 --> 00:11:22,390
and they feed people in areas
where there's nothing to eat.

282
00:11:22,473 --> 00:11:24,183
Ahh.

283
00:11:25,476 --> 00:11:27,686
But she's not the one doing that.

284
00:11:27,770 --> 00:11:28,646
Remember?

285
00:11:30,523 --> 00:11:32,400
Ah, she's the boss there so…

286
00:11:32,483 --> 00:11:33,776
she orders many people around,

287
00:11:33,859 --> 00:11:35,319
and-- and…

288
00:11:35,403 --> 00:11:37,029
she's always in the office.

289
00:11:37,905 --> 00:11:39,407
She's in the highest position.

290
00:11:40,032 --> 00:11:42,535
Oh, wow! That's great.

291
00:11:42,618 --> 00:11:44,286
What's the name of our group again?

292
00:11:44,370 --> 00:11:46,080
Ah, Ja-Ha-Byang!

293
00:11:46,163 --> 00:11:47,915
[tense music playing]

294
00:11:50,376 --> 00:11:51,627
[music fades]

295
00:12:02,763 --> 00:12:05,516
[sneaky music playing]

296
00:12:23,451 --> 00:12:25,327
He is at Room 415.

297
00:12:25,870 --> 00:12:27,746
With only one police escort.

298
00:12:27,830 --> 00:12:28,873
Good.

299
00:12:30,040 --> 00:12:31,750
But we have to be very careful.

300
00:12:32,918 --> 00:12:35,254
We cannot draw too much attention.

301
00:12:35,963 --> 00:12:36,839
Don't worry.

302
00:12:37,631 --> 00:12:39,008
I have what we need.

303
00:12:41,427 --> 00:12:42,428
[pleasant music playing]

304
00:12:42,511 --> 00:12:43,345
[car door lock clicks]

305
00:12:46,265 --> 00:12:48,184
- Aargh!
- Oh no, Sir!

306
00:12:48,267 --> 00:12:49,310
Oh.

307
00:12:49,393 --> 00:12:50,895
You could at least say excuse me!

308
00:12:50,978 --> 00:12:52,062
Did you see what that one did?

309
00:12:52,146 --> 00:12:53,355
Didn't even say sorry!

310
00:12:53,439 --> 00:12:54,356
I'm going to confront that one!

311
00:12:54,440 --> 00:12:56,484
- Hey! Don't!
- Why?

312
00:12:56,567 --> 00:12:57,735
Foreigner!

313
00:12:57,818 --> 00:12:59,236
Do you want a nosebleed?

314
00:12:59,945 --> 00:13:00,779
Okay.

315
00:13:01,447 --> 00:13:02,907
I'm so dirty.

316
00:13:03,449 --> 00:13:05,242
I don't want them to see me like this.

317
00:13:05,784 --> 00:13:06,869
Let's swap jackets.

318
00:13:06,952 --> 00:13:07,912
Pardon?

319
00:13:07,995 --> 00:13:10,122
I just said, let's swap jackets!

320
00:13:10,206 --> 00:13:11,999
I don't like dirty clothes, disgusting.

321
00:13:12,082 --> 00:13:13,667
Yes, Sir.

322
00:13:13,751 --> 00:13:16,170
[music continues]

323
00:13:27,640 --> 00:13:29,058
Sir, help please.

324
00:13:32,520 --> 00:13:34,605
What’s the matter with you?
You're so dirty!

325
00:13:34,688 --> 00:13:36,565
- [music fades]
- Oh my, Ms. Audrey, our feeding program

326
00:13:36,649 --> 00:13:38,317
is still further inside.

327
00:13:38,400 --> 00:13:40,611
Ah. Ah, maybe we should hang

328
00:13:40,694 --> 00:13:43,906
the Harvest Aid International
tarpaulin there, right?

329
00:13:43,989 --> 00:13:46,408
So we have a background for
documentation purposes

330
00:13:46,492 --> 00:13:47,409
when we take pictures.

331
00:13:47,493 --> 00:13:48,744
Oh, you're so good!

332
00:13:48,827 --> 00:13:50,079
- Yes!
- True! Agree.

333
00:13:50,162 --> 00:13:51,247
- Careful there.
- Okay.

334
00:13:51,330 --> 00:13:52,164
There, mmm-hmm.

335
00:13:52,748 --> 00:13:54,083
At least it's complete.

336
00:13:55,167 --> 00:13:56,043
[coughs]

337
00:14:01,090 --> 00:14:04,176
[heavy music playing]

338
00:14:05,886 --> 00:14:07,429
- [thumps & squeals]
- Sorry! Sorry!

339
00:14:07,513 --> 00:14:08,722
WOMAN: Come on, hurry up!

340
00:14:08,806 --> 00:14:09,974
C’mon.

341
00:14:12,226 --> 00:14:15,229
[music swells]

342
00:14:17,773 --> 00:14:20,234
Ms. Audrey! Ms. Audrey.

343
00:14:20,818 --> 00:14:21,861
We’ll pass here.

344
00:14:21,944 --> 00:14:23,112
Come on, let's go.

345
00:14:23,195 --> 00:14:24,446
Coming!

346
00:14:24,530 --> 00:14:26,532
[music swells]

347
00:14:27,116 --> 00:14:30,744
Janine, why did you tell Hailey that…

348
00:14:31,370 --> 00:14:32,746
we're fraternal twins?

349
00:14:33,330 --> 00:14:34,456
Eh, we're not.

350
00:14:35,040 --> 00:14:38,043
Well, I had no choice.

351
00:14:38,669 --> 00:14:41,255
Because I don't want everyone
to know that…

352
00:14:41,338 --> 00:14:42,882
I'm just adopted and…

353
00:14:43,841 --> 00:14:45,092
you're the only OG.

354
00:14:46,677 --> 00:14:49,096
Hmm? There's nothing wrong with that,

355
00:14:49,179 --> 00:14:51,557
and Hailey is already our friend.

356
00:14:52,349 --> 00:14:55,728
So, we shouldn't lie to her.

357
00:14:55,811 --> 00:14:57,771
So, what do you want me to do?

358
00:14:57,855 --> 00:14:58,898
Take it back?

359
00:14:59,940 --> 00:15:03,277
And don't tell Hailey that…

360
00:15:03,360 --> 00:15:04,528
Daddy is just a tailor.

361
00:15:05,112 --> 00:15:06,947
She might think that…

362
00:15:07,781 --> 00:15:08,991
we're poor.

363
00:15:09,074 --> 00:15:10,743
Even if Tatoy is a tailor,

364
00:15:10,826 --> 00:15:12,369
we're not poor.

365
00:15:13,203 --> 00:15:15,539
Besides, what's wrong with being poor?

366
00:15:16,040 --> 00:15:19,501
Oh my, whatever.
We can't take back what…

367
00:15:19,585 --> 00:15:20,419
I already said.

368
00:15:21,086 --> 00:15:22,588
JANINE: Just go with it.

369
00:15:23,339 --> 00:15:24,381
Let's go

370
00:15:24,465 --> 00:15:26,884
Don't add any more made-up stories.

371
00:15:28,385 --> 00:15:29,470
I won't.

372
00:15:30,596 --> 00:15:31,847
Promise, I swear.

373
00:15:33,766 --> 00:15:36,226
[mellow music playing]

374
00:15:39,980 --> 00:15:43,442
Uhm, what was the name of our…

375
00:15:43,525 --> 00:15:44,485
classmate again?

376
00:15:45,444 --> 00:15:47,279
Ibyang, not that I'm criticizing but…

377
00:15:47,947 --> 00:15:49,657
why does it seem like she
doesn't take a bath?

378
00:15:50,240 --> 00:15:51,575
- Shh!
- Because she smells like fish.

379
00:15:52,326 --> 00:15:54,161
Don't say that!

380
00:15:54,244 --> 00:15:55,120
That's bad.

381
00:15:56,497 --> 00:15:57,373
I didn't--

382
00:15:59,208 --> 00:16:00,668
JANINE: She's so sweaty.

383
00:16:00,751 --> 00:16:02,127
I don't know, I pity her.

384
00:16:02,211 --> 00:16:05,089
[music continues]

385
00:16:09,718 --> 00:16:11,595
Uhm, good day!

386
00:16:11,679 --> 00:16:15,683
Ah, did you see the man
wearing a flannel…

387
00:16:15,766 --> 00:16:18,811
polo earlier, checkered?

388
00:16:18,894 --> 00:16:20,521
Ah, the one sitting here,

389
00:16:20,604 --> 00:16:21,480
the one eating.

390
00:16:22,856 --> 00:16:23,857
Ah, the one with a mustache,

391
00:16:23,941 --> 00:16:25,985
the former sol-- soldier?

392
00:16:26,068 --> 00:16:26,902
Yes.

393
00:16:26,986 --> 00:16:27,945
MAN: He already left.

394
00:16:28,445 --> 00:16:30,114
Ah, uhm, is that so?

395
00:16:30,197 --> 00:16:31,865
Uhm, where did he go?

396
00:16:32,741 --> 00:16:33,784
We don't know.

397
00:16:35,327 --> 00:16:36,412
[music continues]

398
00:16:36,495 --> 00:16:38,706
We just bought him food earlier,

399
00:16:38,789 --> 00:16:40,874
because he had no money left for food.

400
00:16:42,126 --> 00:16:43,252
[suspicious music playing]

401
00:16:43,335 --> 00:16:44,586
Okay, thank you.

402
00:16:44,670 --> 00:16:45,671
MAN: All right.

403
00:16:46,422 --> 00:16:47,589
[music continues]

404
00:16:47,673 --> 00:16:49,341
[music fades]

405
00:16:49,425 --> 00:16:51,010
[suspicious music playing]

406
00:17:16,952 --> 00:17:19,079
Where are we going, by the way?

407
00:17:19,163 --> 00:17:20,622
Ah, Brother Atoy asked us

408
00:17:20,706 --> 00:17:22,750
to buy a surgical mask and cap.

409
00:17:22,833 --> 00:17:25,878
Karla: Then he said to meet him
on the 4th floor in 5 minutes.

410
00:17:25,961 --> 00:17:26,879
Let's go.

411
00:17:27,504 --> 00:17:29,548
[music continues]

412
00:17:35,596 --> 00:17:37,264
[music fades]

413
00:17:37,347 --> 00:17:40,517
[high-pitched ping sound]

414
00:17:48,901 --> 00:17:51,987
[suspicious music playing]

415
00:17:59,369 --> 00:18:01,288
[groaning]

416
00:18:02,081 --> 00:18:03,540
[music fades]

417
00:18:04,249 --> 00:18:06,543
[ominous music playing]

418
00:18:14,593 --> 00:18:15,761
[groans]

419
00:18:22,893 --> 00:18:25,104
Ouch.

420
00:18:25,979 --> 00:18:27,272
[groans]

421
00:18:27,356 --> 00:18:28,357
[music continues]

422
00:18:40,494 --> 00:18:41,829
Ah, sir, what's going on?

423
00:18:43,747 --> 00:18:44,998
[music fades]

424
00:18:45,874 --> 00:18:49,169
[foreboding music playing]

425
00:18:57,094 --> 00:18:57,970
Karla: Brother!

426
00:18:58,053 --> 00:18:59,471
Den.

427
00:18:59,555 --> 00:19:01,265
Here's what you asked us to buy.

428
00:19:01,849 --> 00:19:03,600
- Here, wear these.
- DENDEN: Okay.

429
00:19:03,684 --> 00:19:04,893
Ah, we'll put Uno on this.

430
00:19:04,977 --> 00:19:06,979
We'll pretend we're taking him
to get a CT scan,

431
00:19:07,062 --> 00:19:08,564
then we'll take him straight downstairs.

432
00:19:09,148 --> 00:19:10,357
- Okay.
- Okay, good.

433
00:19:10,440 --> 00:19:12,401
Darn. Can this be handwashed?

434
00:19:12,484 --> 00:19:13,819
Have it dry-- have it dry--

435
00:19:14,903 --> 00:19:15,779
It's so sticky.

436
00:19:16,530 --> 00:19:18,407
- Wait.
- [tense music playing]

437
00:19:18,490 --> 00:19:19,491
That's Atoy.

438
00:19:20,450 --> 00:19:23,412
[music swells]

439
00:19:29,918 --> 00:19:31,461
[ominous music playing]

440
00:19:31,545 --> 00:19:33,672
Uhm, we are here to transfer

441
00:19:33,755 --> 00:19:35,549
the patient to another floor.

442
00:19:36,550 --> 00:19:39,845
[tense music playing]

443
00:19:48,187 --> 00:19:49,396
Wait a moment.

444
00:19:51,440 --> 00:19:53,108
- [music continues]
- [groaning]

445
00:19:54,818 --> 00:19:58,739
[groans]

446
00:20:10,083 --> 00:20:11,126
[music fades]

447
00:20:12,961 --> 00:20:13,921
Atoy: It's Matangbaka.

448
00:20:14,004 --> 00:20:15,047
Wait, hold on.

449
00:20:16,840 --> 00:20:18,508
- Huh? Who, Brother?
- Shh, don't-- [shushes].

450
00:20:18,592 --> 00:20:19,635
Just look over there.

451
00:20:19,718 --> 00:20:21,845
[music continues]

452
00:20:21,929 --> 00:20:22,846
Atoy: Matangbaka.

453
00:20:22,930 --> 00:20:23,805
It was Atoy whom I saw,

454
00:20:23,889 --> 00:20:24,890
I'm not mistaken.

455
00:20:29,978 --> 00:20:31,980
[music swells]

456
00:20:35,275 --> 00:20:36,652
There was no notice that

457
00:20:36,735 --> 00:20:38,612
the patient would be transferred.

458
00:20:38,695 --> 00:20:40,113
Do you have a doctor's order?

459
00:20:40,197 --> 00:20:41,114
Of course.

460
00:20:41,198 --> 00:20:42,199
I said I would come here

461
00:20:42,282 --> 00:20:43,992
to Room 415, get the pa--

462
00:20:44,076 --> 00:20:46,119
You know what? Just look on your phone.

463
00:20:46,745 --> 00:20:47,996
[suspenseful music playing]

464
00:20:48,080 --> 00:20:49,748
- [bullet whizzes]
- [groans]

465
00:20:49,831 --> 00:20:54,544
[music continues]

466
00:20:57,756 --> 00:20:58,966
[bullet whizzes]

467
00:20:59,049 --> 00:21:00,092
[music swells]

468
00:21:00,175 --> 00:21:01,051
[gun cocks]

469
00:21:01,134 --> 00:21:02,219
Call security!

470
00:21:02,803 --> 00:21:03,971
- [bullet whizzes]
- [groans] [bullet whizzes]

471
00:21:04,596 --> 00:21:05,764
Got--

472
00:21:05,847 --> 00:21:08,433
[sneaky music playing]

473
00:21:09,101 --> 00:21:10,310
Where's Atoy?

474
00:21:10,394 --> 00:21:11,478
You're with Atoy.

475
00:21:11,561 --> 00:21:13,146
Uh, Atoy?

476
00:21:13,230 --> 00:21:14,564
- ELIAS: Yes.
- Who’s Atoy?

477
00:21:14,648 --> 00:21:17,359
I was just talking to my friend here.

478
00:21:17,442 --> 00:21:18,568
I can't be mistaken.

479
00:21:18,652 --> 00:21:20,279
I'm sure, I saw Atoy, okay.

480
00:21:20,362 --> 00:21:22,698
Do you see these eyes, these big eyes?

481
00:21:22,781 --> 00:21:23,949
These are cow's eyes!

482
00:21:24,032 --> 00:21:25,117
They almost bulge out!

483
00:21:25,200 --> 00:21:27,244
That's why they call me Elias Matangbaka!

484
00:21:27,828 --> 00:21:29,413
Well, it's not like that, Sir.

485
00:21:29,496 --> 00:21:30,998
Maybe your eyes are just big,

486
00:21:31,081 --> 00:21:31,999
because of your age too.

487
00:21:32,082 --> 00:21:33,083
You have cataracts,

488
00:21:33,166 --> 00:21:34,293
your vision is blurred.

489
00:21:34,376 --> 00:21:35,836
That's right, yes.

490
00:21:35,919 --> 00:21:37,254
Shug: Hey!

491
00:21:37,337 --> 00:21:39,589
Even though Sir Elias is a bit old,

492
00:21:40,632 --> 00:21:42,676
his vision is still 20/20.

493
00:21:42,759 --> 00:21:44,177
[smirks]

494
00:21:44,261 --> 00:21:45,679
[heavy music playing]

495
00:21:45,762 --> 00:21:47,848
KARLA: Oh, then nice to
meet you, Sir Baka.

496
00:21:47,931 --> 00:21:48,932
That's it.

497
00:21:49,808 --> 00:21:55,397
[tense music playing]

498
00:21:55,480 --> 00:21:57,482
[music fades]

499
00:21:59,609 --> 00:22:02,946
[foreboding music playing]

500
00:22:17,252 --> 00:22:18,795
- Miss, don't shout!
- [gasps]

501
00:22:18,879 --> 00:22:21,006
Ah, please Ah, please, please.

502
00:22:21,089 --> 00:22:22,341
Let go of me, please.

503
00:22:22,424 --> 00:22:24,176
- Here, here. Eh
- Give me your bag!

504
00:22:24,259 --> 00:22:25,802
- There, there, there!
- Look.

505
00:22:25,886 --> 00:22:26,970
Please, just let me go.

506
00:22:27,054 --> 00:22:28,138
I have a child, please.

507
00:22:28,221 --> 00:22:29,431
Boss, there's nothing inside!

508
00:22:30,140 --> 00:22:31,808
What is this?! This is useless!

509
00:22:31,892 --> 00:22:34,436
- Look, oh! There's an ATM!
- Let's go.

510
00:22:34,519 --> 00:22:35,562
Come on, come with us!

511
00:22:35,645 --> 00:22:36,730
Withdraw from your ATM!

512
00:22:36,813 --> 00:22:37,773
Let's go!

513
00:22:37,856 --> 00:22:40,275
- [heavy music playing]
- [thuds]

514
00:22:42,819 --> 00:22:45,530
[groans]

515
00:22:46,948 --> 00:22:48,408
No, no, no, no, no, no, no!

516
00:22:49,618 --> 00:22:51,244
We need him alive! Let's go!

517
00:22:53,580 --> 00:22:54,873
[music swells]

518
00:22:54,956 --> 00:22:56,541
[groaning]

519
00:22:56,625 --> 00:23:00,420
[music continues]

520
00:23:00,504 --> 00:23:01,546
[music fades]

521
00:23:02,214 --> 00:23:04,424
- Help! Help!
- Psst, hey! Let go of her.

522
00:23:04,508 --> 00:23:06,384
- Oh, my god.
- [rock music playing]

523
00:23:06,468 --> 00:23:07,928
Don't meddle here!

524
00:23:09,054 --> 00:23:10,806
[grunting & groaning]

525
00:23:11,515 --> 00:23:12,974
[thumping, swishing, thudding]

526
00:23:13,058 --> 00:23:14,559
Audrey: Help!

527
00:23:14,643 --> 00:23:17,270
[grunting & groaning]

528
00:23:17,771 --> 00:23:19,564
Go ahead! Go ahead, just try.

529
00:23:19,648 --> 00:23:20,732
[grunts]

530
00:23:20,816 --> 00:23:21,691
[thumps]

531
00:23:21,775 --> 00:23:22,692
Audrey: Help!

532
00:23:22,776 --> 00:23:23,819
[thuds]

533
00:23:23,902 --> 00:23:25,028
- [swishes & groans]
- Audrey: Oscar--

534
00:23:25,112 --> 00:23:26,696
- Help!
- Robber: You're brave, huh!

535
00:23:26,780 --> 00:23:27,948
Help!

536
00:23:28,031 --> 00:23:29,658
[grunts, thumps & groans]
Audrey: Help! Help!

537
00:23:29,741 --> 00:23:30,867
Audrey: Oscar!

538
00:23:32,035 --> 00:23:33,495
Hey! What is that?!

539
00:23:33,578 --> 00:23:34,538
Enough!

540
00:23:34,621 --> 00:23:35,705
[groans]

541
00:23:35,789 --> 00:23:37,582
Oh, he-- he needs to be taken
to the hospital!

542
00:23:37,666 --> 00:23:38,917
Sir, are you okay?

543
00:23:39,000 --> 00:23:41,294
- [groans]
- Please get up.

544
00:23:41,378 --> 00:23:43,588
[tense music playing]

545
00:23:44,089 --> 00:23:45,215
You, ma'am, are you wounded po, ma'am?

546
00:23:45,298 --> 00:23:46,508
- No, I'm okay.
- All right.

547
00:23:46,591 --> 00:23:48,260
Let's take him to the hospital, quick.

548
00:23:49,052 --> 00:23:49,970
NURSE: Sir, Sir, Sir!

549
00:23:50,053 --> 00:23:50,971
[screaming & panicking nearby]

550
00:23:51,054 --> 00:23:53,473
Someone is shooting in patient
Alcaraz’s room!

551
00:23:54,141 --> 00:23:56,560
The cop who was guarding
him is already dead.

552
00:23:56,643 --> 00:23:57,853
Call the police!

553
00:23:58,562 --> 00:23:59,521
Sir!

554
00:24:00,105 --> 00:24:01,022
Oh, I'm a police officer.

555
00:24:01,106 --> 00:24:02,899
Come on, come on!

556
00:24:02,983 --> 00:24:04,359
[rousing music playing]

557
00:24:05,318 --> 00:24:09,990
[electronic blipping]

558
00:24:10,073 --> 00:24:14,161
[intense music playing]

559
00:24:16,246 --> 00:24:20,083
Atoy, I'm with Oscar at the hospital now.

560
00:24:20,167 --> 00:24:22,961
Audrey on the phone: He was stabbed,
while saving me.

561
00:24:23,044 --> 00:24:24,796
Atoy again and again.

562
00:24:24,880 --> 00:24:26,298
Artem: We must kill that guy!

563
00:24:26,381 --> 00:24:30,093
First, we must handle Uno Alcaraz.

564
00:24:30,177 --> 00:24:32,512
He knows who Belladonna is.

565
00:24:33,471 --> 00:24:36,016
That is our focus.

566
00:24:36,099 --> 00:24:36,975
Uno!

567
00:24:37,058 --> 00:24:38,435
- EMERSON: What?
- Uno is missing!

568
00:24:38,518 --> 00:24:40,228
He escaped from the hospital,

569
00:24:40,312 --> 00:24:41,354
before Samir could get him!

570
00:24:41,438 --> 00:24:43,356
Is our big-time mission.

571
00:24:44,441 --> 00:24:48,195
O.H.U. Operation Finding Uno!

572
00:24:48,278 --> 00:24:50,530
How? Where will you stay now?

573
00:24:50,614 --> 00:24:52,157
It's okay, don't worry about that.

574
00:24:52,240 --> 00:24:53,950
If you have nowhere else to stay,

575
00:24:54,910 --> 00:24:56,453
maybe you'd like…

576
00:24:56,536 --> 00:24:57,579
to stay with us for now?

577
00:24:58,121 --> 00:24:59,539
♪ Like a bubble, like a bubble ♪

578
00:24:59,623 --> 00:25:00,999
♪ If the cutter,

579
00:25:01,082 --> 00:25:02,083
knows how to fix ♪

580
00:25:02,167 --> 00:25:05,629
[“Mamang Sastre” playing]

581
00:25:08,381 --> 00:25:09,216
(Fix this)
